# LangLearn configuration
# Copy this file to .env and adjust values. Exporting the same vars
# in the shell overrides these values.

# --- LLM (OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions API) ---
# Required. Get yours from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Point this at any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (OpenAI, Azure, local proxy, ...)
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Ollama (local) ---
# Uncomment these lines to use Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint instead of
# OpenAI. No API key needed. Start "ollama serve" and pull a model first.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=llama3.1

# --- Server ---
# PORT=5056
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# LANGLEARN_DATA_DIR=./data
# FLASK_DEBUG=0

# --- Auth gate (optional) ---
# Set a password to require sign-in for the entire app. Leave blank or unset
# to keep the app open (default for local single-user use). The value is
# read on every login attempt — never written to SQLite — and rotation
# takes effect on the next login after changing this file and restarting.
# The cookie's Secure flag is auto-detected from the request (HTTPS, proxy
# X-Forwarded-Proto, or public-domain Host header) so no extra env vars
# are needed for either LAN or public-domain use.
# LANGLEARN_PASSWORD=changeme